From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A7om <hatter6822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: Add the Broadcom BCM2712 SoC

The BCM2712 of the Raspberry Pi 5 has four Cortex-A76 cores, a GIC-400
and a mix of Broadcom set-top-box and VideoCore peripherals. Unlike the
BCM283x SoCs, its peripherals sit above 4 GiB (0x10_0000_0000 up), and
the legacy ARM control block is gone.

Model the SoC with the devices a bare-metal kernel or Linux needs to
boot: the cores (MPIDR.Aff1 is the core number, CNTFRQ is 54 MHz,
optional EL3), the GIC-400 with 288 SPIs and the timer and maintenance
PPIs, UART10 (a PL011) and UARTA (a 16550 with its registers 4 bytes
apart), the system timer, the watchdog and reset status block, the
RNG200, the seven level 2 interrupt controllers, the two GPIO blocks and
their pin controllers, the HDMI ports' two DDC I2C controllers, the two
SD/eMMC host controllers, and the VideoCore mailbox with the firmware
property and framebuffer channels. UART10 is the first serial port and
UARTA the second. The first SD host's bus is the SoC's sd-bus, for the
board's card slot. The firmware reaches buffers through a VideoCore bus
view that holds the first GiB of RAM at 0x0 and at 0xc000_0000. Every
other block in the device tree is an unimplemented-device placeholder of
its size, and two catch-all windows log accesses anywhere else in the
peripheral ranges.

bcm2712_fdt_populate() describes the modelled devices in a device tree,
from the same constants as the memory map, for boards that generate one.
The second SD host serves the Pi 5's Wi-Fi radio, so its node is left
for the board to enable.

Addresses, interrupts and compatibles follow Linux's bcm2712.dtsi;
values not documented publicly are marked for checking on hardware.
---
 hw/arm/Kconfig     | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 hw/arm/meson.build |  1 +
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/arm/Kconfig b/hw/arm/Kconfig
index 16f83f09..868fe17b 100644
--- a/hw/arm/Kconfig
+++ b/hw/arm/Kconfig
@@ -384,6 +384,27 @@ config RASPI
     select BCM2836_CONTROL
     select BCM2838_GPIO
 
+config BCM2712
+    bool
+    select ARM_GIC
+    select BCM2711_AVS_MONITOR
+    select BCM2711_RNG200
+    select BCM2712_PROPERTY
+    select BCM2712_SDHCI
+    select BCM2835_FB
+    select BCM2835_MBOX
+    select BCM2835_OTP
+    select BCM2835_POWERMGT
+    select BCM2835_SYSTMR
+    select BRCMSTB_GPIO
+    select BRCMSTB_I2C
+    select BRCMSTB_L2_INTC
+    select BRCMSTB_PINCTRL
+    select DEVICE_TREE
+    select PL011 # UART10
+    select SERIAL_MM # UARTA
+    select UNIMP
+
 config STM32F100_SOC
     bool
     select ARM_V7M
diff --git a/hw/arm/meson.build b/hw/arm/meson.build
index 4233a800..00b030ab 100644
--- a/hw/arm/meson.build
+++ b/hw/arm/meson.build
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ arm_common_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_RASPI', if_true: files(
   'raspi.c',
   'raspi4b.c'
 ))
+arm_common_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_BCM2712', if_true: files('bcm2712.c'))
 arm_common_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_STM32F100_SOC', if_true: files('stm32f100_soc.c'))
 arm_common_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_STM32F205_SOC', if_true: files('stm32f205_soc.c'))
 arm_common_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_STM32F405_SOC', if_true: files('stm32f405_soc.c'))
